<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Themistoklis Sofoulis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860–1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Themistoklis Sofoulis was a Greek politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a>. An archaeologist by training, he led the rising on Samos in 1912 that expelled the last Ottoman garrison and brought the island's union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. He later led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a> after Venizelos and was Prime Minister of Greece in 1924 and again from 1945 to 1946 and 1947 to 1949.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/themistoklis-sofoulis.jpg" alt="Themistoklis Sofoulis" width="250" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Themistoklis_Sofoulis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
